Three related fixes in LandscapePlayer:

- The cover-art BoxWithConstraints had contentAlignment = Center but
  no fillMaxHeight, so a Row's default top-alignment left it hugging
  the top whenever the thumbnail was shorter than the full row -
  centering only ever applied within whatever (possibly short) bounds
  the box ended up with.
- The controls column centered itself with a weighted-spacer sandwich
  around a single child; replaced with a plain Arrangement.Center so
  it doesn't silently stop centering the day a second sibling lands
  there.
- The queue handle wasn't missing so much as invisible: collapsedBound
  equaled dismissedBound, i.e. zero peek height, so the sheet's own
  full-width collapsed content (which already spans the whole player,
  not just the controls column) had nothing to render. A separate,
  narrower "queue hint" row had been added inside the controls column
  as a workaround - removed now that the sheet's real handle has a
  height to show up in, matching PortraitPlayer's collapsedBound.
