From e797442862bf0157d8845f1ae9cd6aabca2a2596 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 15:39:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 056/180] Rework the equalizer into a full-screen panel, and
 add balance/more presets

The EQ sheet's state used to live inside the transient 3-dot menu
popup that opened it, so a track change or closing the menu tore it
down along with everything else. Move it to EqualizerPanelState, a
CompositionLocal provided once at the top of the composition tree
(same pattern as LocalMenuState) - the button beside the like button,
the pull-down handle above the cover art, and the 3-dot menu entry all
just flip the same shared flag now, and the panel itself lives beside
BottomSheetPlayer's other overlays, not inside a popup.

Also, since it's full-screen now instead of a sheet peeking up from
the bottom:
- Renders the player's own background (whatever style is active)
  instead of a flat surface colour.
- The band strip is a LazyRow at a fixed per-band width rather than a
  plain Row squeezed to the screen width, so it can run wider than the
  screen and scroll sideways - Poweramp-style - instead of every band
  fighting for a sliver of a 6-inch phone.
- Tapping a band's own frequency label opens its advanced editor now,
  replacing the separate row of selector chips that was overflowing
  off-screen with nothing to scroll it.
- Added a basic playback transport (prev/play-pause/next) so the panel
  doesn't have to be closed just to skip a track.
- Added a left/right balance slider (standard attenuate-the-far-side
  law, applied post-EQ per channel in EqualizerAudioProcessor).
- Expanded the presets from 4 to 12 (Poweramp-style genre set: Pop,
  Rock, Classical, Jazz, Dance, Hip-Hop, Acoustic, Loudness, alongside
  the originals).
- Dropped Squiggly from the EQ's own slider-style choice - its wave
  animation is driven by playback progress, which a gain slider has
  no equivalent of, so it only ever rendered as a flat line anyway.

Two new settings (Player settings) let the button and handle be
toggled independently: show_equalizer_button / show_equalizer_handle,
both on by default.
