Subject: [PATCH 076/180] Add dial/slider toggle, Poweramp-style flat sliders,
 and value color gradient to the equalizer

- New 'Use dials instead of sliders' setting: band gain, the band editor's frequency/gain, and bass/treble all switch between the rotary dials and a slider depending on it, alongside the existing separate balance dial/slider toggle.
- Every EQ slider (band gain, frequency/gain in slider mode, Q, balance, and all five compressor controls) now uses a Poweramp-style rounded-rect channel with a flat handle (PowerampTrack/PowerampThumb) instead of Material3's default thin line and circular thumb.
- New 'Color by value (green to red)' setting: colors each control - dial arc or slider track/thumb - on a gradient from green at the low end of its range to red at the high end, instead of the flat contrast/theme color.
VerticalSlider now takes a required thumb slot alongside its existing required track slot, matching the same 'no sensible default, every caller has an opinion' reasoning.
