From c1ecd79807f76e86a6a98d38f28cb5fecac21ed5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 15:38:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 080/180] EQ tone controls rework, Liquid background v3,
 per-style text contrast

- Bass/Treble dials now move every band at/below 250Hz or at/above
  4kHz together (a real tone-control shelf), instead of only the single
  lowest/highest band. Balance moved into the same row as a dial,
  evenly spaced across the full width; the old standalone balance
  section (and its slider/dial toggle) is gone.
- Mini transport reverted to its original size.
- Compressor dials enlarged slightly along with bass/treble/balance;
  band-strip gain controls always render as sliders regardless of the
  dial/slider setting, matching the reference layout.
- LiquidBackground rewritten again: the spiky path-based "ferrofluid"
  shape is gone. Back to soft drifting blobs, but using real
  Material/album colors instead of a black-lerped tint, a smaller
  footprint so it reads as contained rather than covering the screen, a
  per-launch random phase so the arrangement differs every app start,
  and stronger audio weighting for a tighter sync.
- Added a Liquid colour scheme setting (theme surface / black / white
  backdrop) and a Liquid-specific auto text contrast toggle, independent
  of the existing Frosted/Blur one - rememberPlayerOnBackgroundColor now
  takes the active player background style so it can pick the right
  preference, wired through Player.kt, EqualizerPanel.kt, Queue.kt and
  Lyrics.kt.
