top settings, tone controls + profiles, frequency bands (strip and the
selected band's editor), and the compressor. Against a busy Liquid/
Blur background especially, a hairline HorizontalDivider was easy to
miss; a whole card is not. Cards are translucent
(surfaceContainer at 0.6 alpha), so the panel still reads as floating
over the player background rather than paving over it.

Profiles (the built-in/saved preset chips, plus export/import) moved
into the tone-controls card rather than sitting between the top
toggles and the tone controls: both are "how the curve gets shaped",
which is a different question from the curve itself (the frequency-
band card).

Also closed three places that ignored the "use cover contrast color"
setting and used a fixed theme color regardless:
- BandColumn's selected-band highlight (border + label) used
  MaterialTheme.colorScheme.primary unconditionally - the one part of
  the panel that didn't follow the toggle everything else does.
- The profile FilterChips had no colors override at all, so they used
  Material3's stock (theme-only) chip colors.
