From bee6a32d7f99b198186e56a7666873e42e027a96 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 14:35:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 097/180] Fix Liquid's Theme-surface contrast being a no-op,
 and its flat-black look

rememberPlayerOnBackgroundColor's SURFACE branch returned themeFallback
- the exact same value the toggle-off branch two lines above it
already returns - so switching "Auto text contrast" on and off did
nothing whenever Liquid's backdrop was Theme surface, which is the
default. Surface has a real, known colour just like black/white do:
now measures the actual elevated surface tone Player.kt paints and
picks light/dark text from its measured luminance, instead of guessing
from "dark theme implies dark surface" - a guess dynamic per-song
theming isn't guaranteed to agree with.

Separately: that elevated tone was computed at NavigationBarDefaults.
Elevation (3dp), the same subtle tint used everywhere else - but
Material3's dark-theme surface is already close to black on its own,
so at 3dp the primary tint blended in was too faint to read as
"themed" rather than flat black. That's what made Theme surface look
like a plain black/pure-black backdrop even with Pure Black off.
Raised to a dedicated, clearly-visible elevation (LiquidSurfaceElevation,
16dp) for Liquid's surface backdrop specifically - every other style
keeps the original subtle one. The contrast measurement above reads
this same constant, not a second copy, so the two can't drift apart.
