From 6688e44da03f6976067974216a7e2ea98b376633 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 12:38:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 109/180] Fix repeat button drifting from the right edge when
 seek buttons toggle

Each control-row icon (shuffle, skip, seek, repeat) sat in its own
Modifier.weight(1f) Box with no contentAlignment, defaulting to TopStart -
so every icon was flush against the *left* edge of its own slot rather than
centered. Shuffle's slot is the row's first, so that flush-left default
happens to put it right at the row's true left edge either way. Repeat's
isn't: it's flush-left within the *last* slot, leaving a (slot width - icon
width) gap between it and the row's true right edge - and that gap's size
depends on how many slots there are, so it visibly changes size (making
repeat look like it's slid) whenever seek forward/back are toggled on or
off, since that changes the slot count from 4 to 6 and back.

Centering each icon in its slot, matching the pattern Queue.kt's own
transport row already uses, makes the left and right margins mirror each
other regardless of how many buttons are currently shown - so toggling seek
increment no longer moves repeat relative to the edge. Applied the same fix
to the granular custom-layout grouped-row case, which had the identical Box
without contentAlignment.

