From 5471b826b4ebfdc678da1edb824f634446e50263 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 21:50:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 111/180] Fix lyrics rendering silently dying partway through a
 song

Two separate LaunchedEffects, both keyed on lyricsModel, own two different
sources of truth: one populates the `lines` snapshot list, the other (the
refresh loop driving currentLineIndex) only checks lyricsModel's own .text
before entering its while(isActive) loop. If `lines` was ever momentarily
out of step with that check - e.g. a fast song change - findCurrentLineIndex
indexed into an empty list (lines[lines.lastIndex] on lastIndex == -1) and
threw, which killed that loop's coroutine for good. Nothing restarts a
LaunchedEffect keyed only on lyricsModel until the model itself changes
again, so from the user's side lyrics just stopped advancing mid-song and
no setting could bring it back - toggling settings doesn't touch this key.

Three defenses, cheapest first: findCurrentLineIndex returns -1 for an
empty list instead of indexing into it; the refresh loop's body runs inside
runCatching so any other future edge case can't kill the loop for the rest
of the song either; and the scroll effect's calculateOffset() uses
lines.getOrNull(currentLineIndex) instead of a hard index, since a stale
currentLineIndex against a shorter list right after a song change hit the
exact same crash pattern.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
