Subject: [PATCH 117/180] Use a PoToken-bearing client for playback streams

Every PoToken fix in this series so far - the session rotation, the 40s
cache cap, invalidate()-before-refresh - operated on a token that was
never in the URL being played. MAIN_CLIENT was ANDROID_VR_NO_AUTH, which
leaves useWebPoTokens at its false default, so

    if (client.useWebPoTokens && webStreamingPot != null)

never fired for the client that actually won selection.

That is the missing piece behind the invariance those commits kept
running into: the failure point didn't move for chunk size, for
connection duration, or for token freshness because none of those
touched what was on the wire. The stream being played carried no pot at
all, and googlevideo cuts such a stream at the first continuation
request - which is why playback consistently started clean and died the
moment the first chunk ran out.

Promotes WEB_REMIX (useWebPoTokens = true) to MAIN_CLIENT and demotes
ANDROID_VR_NO_AUTH to a fallback. WEB_REMIX also requires working
signature deobfuscation, which SignatureCipherManager already provides
via the WebView path in findUrlOrNull().
