From f6674d826b1e2e9ac4a6fc4239ec6c70c56f8958 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 21:34:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 119/180] Send Referer/Origin on stream requests, precache the
 next song's URL

Every stream request only ever carried a User-Agent. googlevideo.com has
also been observed checking Referer/Origin against the client a URL was
signed for - relevant now that WEB_REMIX (a browser-origin client, not a
native app one) is MAIN_CLIENT. PlaybackData/CachedStreamUrl now carry a
full per-client header map (User-Agent + Referer + Origin) instead of
just a User-Agent string, built by a new YTPlayerUtils.streamHeaders()
matched to the resolved client (music.youtube.com for WEB_REMIX,
www.youtube.com otherwise) and threaded through both MusicService and
DownloadUtil.

Also adds an Experimental toggle (on by default) that precaches the next
song's stream shortly before the current one ends, timed to land inside
the existing 40s PoToken freshness window rather than resolving at the
track transition - one extra request per song, spread out over the
queue instead of clustered at each change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
