From 451a6e8b49d26c69edb92ad980fbae38514a930d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 21:20:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 122/180] Swiping the mini player down stops playback and
 dismisses it

The mini player and the full player share one dismiss gesture (drag past
the mini player height), which used to always just collapse back to the
mini player - added after a hard fling from the FULL player could
overshoot into dismissed territory and tear down playback when the user
only meant to collapse it.

BottomSheetState now records whether the drag that's ending started from
the collapsed (mini player) height. Only that case - an actual swipe
starting on the mini player itself - calls softKillPlayer(); a dismiss
reached from the expanded player still just collapses, unchanged.

