From 16f95c74a4838544206a179b7943f7361d45e067 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 20:19:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 124/180] Update stale client versions/UAs, fix client flags,
 tune HTTP client

Several clients were up to a year out of date: WEB/WEB_REMIX/WEB_CREATOR/
TVHTML5 client versions and the shared Firefox UA all trailed Metrolist's
current values by ~7-11 months; IOS/ANDROID similarly. Old client-version/
UA combinations are a known trigger for degraded player responses as
YouTube ages out old client builds.

Also: WEB_CREATOR and TVHTML5 were missing useWebPoTokens=true; TVHTML5
and TVHTML5_SIMPLY_EMBEDDED_PLAYER had loginRequired=true despite neither
actually requiring it (the latter's whole purpose is a logged-out age-
restriction bypass, which that flag defeated). Context.Client gained
userAgent/osName/deviceMake/deviceModel/androidSdkVersion fields (real
TV/VR clients embed these in the request body, not just headers), wired
through a new YouTubeClient.includeUserAgentInContext flag, and set on
ANDROID_VR_NO_AUTH. Added ANDROID_VR_1_43_32 (non-adaptive bitrate,
fixes YT Music audio stuttering some devices see on the adaptive variant)
as a defined-but-not-yet-wired-in fallback option.

InnerTube's OkHttp client had no explicit timeouts (ktor's default is
none at all - a stalled mobile connection could hang indefinitely) or
connection-pool tuning, and no retry for transient I/O errors/5xx -
