From 9c344b74223718c978358fd21cc85f841980b9cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 21:27:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 132/180] Make AutoEQ search actually search and apply real
 curves

Replaces the AutoEQ placeholder with a working implementation: searches
oratory1990's measurements (AutoEQ's most consistently-referenced single
source) live against GitHub's own API rather than bundling a snapshot of
AutoEQ's 8000+-entry, ~20-source database or standing up infrastructure
to serve it - no bundled data to go stale, no APK size cost, at the cost
of covering one source instead of all of them and needing a network
connection.

New AutoEqRepository: search() lists oratory1990's over-ear/in-ear/earbud
folders via GitHub's contents API and filters client-side; fetchCurve()
downloads and parses the chosen headphone's ParametricEQ.txt (the same
"Preamp: X dB" / "Filter N: ON <type> Fc <freq> Hz Gain <gain> dB Q <q>"
format Equalizer APO and similar tools already use) into an
EqualizerSettings curve, folding AutoEQ's preamp into each band's own
gain since this app's model has no separate preamp field.

The search dialog is now live: debounced search-as-you-type, a results
list grouped by category, and tapping a result fetches, parses, and
applies it in place (keeping the current balance/compressor settings).

