From 303b09707ae8ba1844444c2a81e75e544a38b401 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 21:39:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 134/180] Fix compile error: Coil3's Chain.proceed() takes no
 arguments

Interceptor.Chain.proceed() is a no-arg suspend fun in Coil3 - to
actually change the request before proceeding, the chain itself has to
be replaced first via withRequest(), then proceed() called on that new
chain. The original commit assumed a proceed(request) overload (the
pattern in some older Coil versions/other interceptor APIs) that
doesn't exist here, confirmed by the actual build failure:

  e: ArtworkFallbackInterceptor.kt:28:36 Too many arguments for
     'suspend fun proceed(): ImageResult'.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
