over the database, but nothing ever refreshes that cached copy once a song
is queued - so a song downloaded (or finished downloading) after being
added to the queue kept its stale localPath=null forever, and the player
silently kept re-streaming it instead of switching to the now-available
local file. Only rebuilding the queue from scratch (e.g. re-opening the
playlist) picked up the download. A null localPath from the queue is now
re-checked against the database once before falling through to streaming.
