From 8db6b82bb470773037b281c10e81da827c12142e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 18:57:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 140/180] Strip/dedupe " - Topic" artist credits, clean up ones
 already added

ArtistCreditEnricher resolves featured/split-credit artist names via YT
search, but an artist with no official channel is only findable under
YouTube's auto-generated "X - Topic" channel - so it credited songs with
that raw channel title. When the real artist "X" was already credited on
the same song from elsewhere, this showed up as two separate chips: "X"
and "X - Topic".

Going forward, resolution now strips that suffix and, if an artist already
exists in the database under the clean name, reuses it instead of minting
a second entity for the same real-world artist.

For credits already added before this fix, MIGRATION_22_23 does a one-time
local cleanup: any artist named "X - Topic" gets merged into an existing
"X" (moving its song credits over, dropping the ones that would collide
with a song already crediting both) or, if there's no separate "X", just
has its own name cleaned up in place. Pure SQL against the local database -
no network calls, so it doesn't touch YouTube's API quota.
---
