From 5de846af1942a948e7c7a633cb352b94e419e35a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 12:21:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 148/180] Watch for a dead Discord RPC connection and
 force-reconnect it

Kizzy's isRpcRunning()/isWebSocketConnected() only reflect whether connect()
was called and close() hasn't been - they can't see a socket the OS silently
dropped without a close frame, which routinely happens to an idle connection
after screen-off/Doze on mobile data. When that happens, the gateway socket
object still looks "connected" to every check available, so the existing
token/enable-switch rebuild path never fires and the presence Discord is
showing just stops updating for good, with nothing in the app any wiser.

There's no reliable way to observe the drop itself from here (kizzy doesn't
surface a liveness signal beyond that same dumb flag), so instead of trying
to detect it, a watchdog now force-closes and reopens the connection every
10 minutes while a song is actually playing - the one situation where a
stuck presence would actually be visibly wrong. Extracted the existing
close-then-recreate-then-push logic (previously only run on a token/switch
change) into rebuildDiscordRpc() so both paths share it.
