From b2d95a3e27422742d000ce9bc4ca42d51070a3e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 21:39:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 154/180] Recover the dropped v24 Topic-suffix work, so
 version-24 backups are compatible again

A prior session's last 5 commits on this branch never actually made it into
this branch's committed history - only their regenerated patch file was left
behind, uncommitted (found stashed at the start of tonight's session). One
of those bumped MUSIC_DATABASE_VERSION to 24; since this branch stayed at
23, a backup or an on-disk database from that build reads as "newer than
this app" and gets rejected/crash-looped, which is exactly the "old backups
aren't compatible" and "migration from 24 to 23" issue tonight surfaced.

Recovered the two commits that account for the version bump (skipped three
unrelated ones from that same lost sequence - a VISIONOS client change, an
audio-offload/equalizer conflict fix, and a schema-snapshot/thumbnail-crop/
download-status bundle - none of which this fix depends on, and pulling them
in blind would be scope creep beyond what broke):

- Strip/dedupe "- Topic" credits in the general sync path (DatabaseDao,
  AlbumsDao), not just in ArtistCreditEnricher's own narrow paths - shared
  the Topic-suffix regex/stripping into db/ArtistTopicSuffix.kt, and added
  ArtistsDao.insertOrHealArtist so a *stale* "- Topic" name already stored
  under an id gets corrected instead of silently no-op'd by insert()'s
  OnConflictStrategy.IGNORE.
- MIGRATION_23_24: re-runs the same cleanup MIGRATION_22_23 already does
  (factored into a shared mergeTopicSuffixedArtists, now also covering
  album_artist_map duplicates, which the original migration missed), since
  a database already recorded at version 23 never re-runs a migration
  targeting 23 again no matter how that migration's code changes later.

Reconciled against tonight's own changes: MIGRATION_21_22 and the
downgrade-fallback added earlier this session are untouched and still run
before/alongside this.
