Android 14+ refuses adb install -d (downgrade) unless the *currently
installed* APK is debuggable, regardless of what flags the new install
uses. userdebug already exists as a release-equivalent (same signing
config, no minify) variant for cases like this - it just never actually
set isDebuggable, so it was exactly as downgrade-locked as a real release
build. Left the real release build type alone; userdebug covers this.

