From 0780a40dd9f0d29fc176e6b3d1ab691d76402d0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 13:11:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 165/180] Fix backup creation: run the WAL checkpoint before
 the transaction, not inside it

9fe9e9f9 wrapped both the checkpoint and the file copy in
MusicDatabase.runInTransaction to fix a torn-snapshot race, but SQLite
refuses PRAGMA wal_checkpoint while a transaction is already open on the
same connection - there's nothing for it to do there, since a checkpoint
moves committed WAL frames into the main file and a transaction (open or
not) can't be checkpointed mid-flight. That made every backup attempt
throw instead of actually checkpointing anything, so both manual and
automatic backup creation failed outright.

Moves the checkpoint back out to run before runInTransaction starts,
keeping only the raw file copy inside it - which is all that was ever
needed to close the original race (nothing can write mid-copy once the
transaction holds the writer connection). A write landing in the now-
reopened gap between checkpoint and transaction just stays in the WAL,
excluded from this backup rather than tearing it - equivalent to the
backup having been taken a moment earlier.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../com/dd3boh/outertune/db/MusicDatabase.kt  |  7 +++--
