From faabd682436dc82e1563da5cb56cebe5c001da4f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 21:41:31 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 175/180] Never stream from WEB_REMIX; metadata only. Back off
 when Google throttles.

Two problems, one cause: request volume.

WEB_REMIX was in the stream chain, and its URLs are the short-lived ones
googlevideo serves for about a minute and then refuses. So every time
VISIONOS was skipped, playback quietly got a URL guaranteed to die mid-track
- which reads as "VISIONOS doesn't work" when what actually happened was
"VISIONOS was passed over and WEB_REMIX took the stream". WEB_REMIX is now
metadata-only and not in the stream chain at all; mainPlayerResponse still
supplies every bit of metadata, so nothing login-gated changes. Streams and
downloads both go through this same chain, so both are covered.

The chain is also back to three clients (VISIONOS, two ANDROID_VR builds).
IOS is out - its music URLs are exactly the die-partway-through kind - and so
is the second validation probe I added earlier.

The 403 in the logs was not a per-video bot check, it was Google's
network-level abuse page: "your computer or network may be sending automated
queries". That is this IP being throttled, and the app was earning it. Worst
case per song had become six clients x up to five source-error retries, ~30
player POSTs, each failure triggering more retries - so once throttled,
everything failed, which caused more retries, which deepened the throttle.
Now: that response is recognised, the chain stops immediately instead of
asking five more clients that will all get the same answer, player requests
pause for five minutes so the throttle can decay, and the retry cap is 2
rather than 5 (each retry is a whole chain, not one request).

Also logs each client as it is tried, at warn, so a release logcat shows
whether VISIONOS was reached at all rather than leaving it to be inferred.
